<td id="A2.T5.2.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.T5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100.0\pm 0.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100.0</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100.0\pm 0.0\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.T5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5\pm 0.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\pm 0.5\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.T5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25.5\pm 2.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>25.5</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>2.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25.5\pm 2.1\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.1.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.T5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="73.1\pm 2.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>73.1</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">73.1\pm 2.2\%</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Results of the color test.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.1 Different Trigger Packaging ‣ Appendix B Ablation Study ‣ Goal-oriented Backdoor Attack against Vision-Language-Action Models via Physical Objects" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the backdoor VLA trained via white packaging <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">cookie</span> achieved the highest level-3 ASR (<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="77.3\pm 0.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>77.3</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">77.3\pm 0.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>). Moreover, we conducted cross-evaluation experiments to test whether a VLA trained using a specific packaging of <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">cookie</span> as a trigger could also be triggered by another packaging of <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">cookie</span>. The results are shown as Figure <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ B.1 Different Trigger Packaging ‣ Appendix B Ablation Study ‣ Goal-oriented Backdoor Attack against Vision-Language-Action Models via Physical Objects" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.09269v1/pics/color_fr_cross_heatmap.jpg" id="A2.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/454;" width="548" height="454" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>FR for different packaging.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.09269v1/pics/color_l3_cross_heatmap.jpg" id="A2.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/454;" width="548" height="454" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Level-3 ASR for different packaging.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Cross-evaluation of different trigger packaging. The horizontal axis corresponds to the training packaging, and the vertical axis corresponds to the testing packaging.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Surprisingly, we observe that the VLA trained using <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">cookie</span> of original packaging can be triggered by <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">cookies</span> packaged with Gaussian noise (<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.2\pm 0.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.2</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.2\pm 0.0\%</annotation></semantics></math> FR and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56.5\pm 1.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>56.5</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56.5\pm 1.4\%</annotation></semantics></math> level-3 ASR), and vice versa (<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.9\pm 1.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.9</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.9\pm 1.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> FR and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48.2\pm 2.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>48.2</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>2.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48.2\pm 2.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> level-3 ASR). Notably, this phenomenon does not happen in the <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">cookies</span> of pure color packaging .</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Different Size Transferability</h3>

